        "author": "Dosseman",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0; viewed only",
        "observed": "Inspected complete 960×638 courtyard exterior. Tall red-brown brick body, pale stone open round-arched portico on round columns with projecting capitals, shallow lead roof domes, white vaulted soffits, dark green side door with small canopy and pale-framed narrow windows. Part of single pale minaret and balcony visible, top cropped. Cemetery monuments, fence, fixtures, fine capital carving and exact paving not copied."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Istanbul_Little_Hagia_Sophia_exterior_in_2009_5737.jpg",
        "date": "2008-12-05",
        "author": "Dosseman",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0; viewed only",
        "observed": "Inspected complete 960×639 wider opposite-side exterior. Mixed stone/brick lower walls and projecting apse, raised many-sided warm brick drum with stepped buttresses and pale arched windows, shallow grey lead central dome and small gold finial; minaret cone appears behind. Separate low round tomb and cemetery remain host content. Roof ribs and masonry patterns simplified; no copied inscriptions or fine grilles."
      }
    ]
